<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12073" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπήνη</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>four-wheeled
			wagon,</i> drawn by mules, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμίονοι ἕλκον τετράκυκλον ἀπήνην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					24.324
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				6.57
			</span></i> with <i><span class="en">
				69
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				72
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				73
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				82
			</span></i>; much the same as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅμαξα,</span>
			cf. <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.266
			</span></i> with <i><span class="en">
				324
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				6.72
			</span></i> with <i><span class="en">
				73
			</span></i>: of a <i>racing-car,</i> drawn by mules, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμιόνοις ξεστᾷ τ᾽ ἀπήνᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					4.94
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>O.</u>
				5.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				568
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦν γὰρ δὴ ἀπήνη . . ἡμιόνους ἀνθ᾽
					ἵππων ἔχουσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paus.
					5.9.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> later, any
				<i>car</i> or <i>chariot,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				906
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				753
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πωλική</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				803
			</span></i>; <i>war-chariot,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				4.5.2
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καπάνα.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph., <i>any
				conveyance,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νατα ἀ.</span>”
				<i>ship,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					1123
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλωταῖς ἀπήνῃσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Lyr.Adesp.</u>
					117
				</span></i>
			 ( =
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Trag.Adesp.</u>
				142
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετραβάμονος ὡς ὑπ᾽
			ἀπήνας,</span> of the Trojan horse, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				517
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			metaph., 
				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζεῦγος</span>
			, <i>pair,</i> e.g. of brothers, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ὁμόπτερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					329
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b> in pl.,
			the <i>alae nasi,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.80
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
